{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And also the hand of HaShem, etc., to strike them down.</b> The meaning is: besides the death itself, they still had no rest of spirit in the wilderness, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Bamidbar Rabbah 19:21) that they were bewildered, astordidos (confounded), in the thirty-eight years, and they kept swarming and wandering with illnesses until they were consumed. And the verse's saying <b>from the midst of the camp</b> means that HaShem distinguished between those upon whom the decree had been pronounced and the rest of the camp: those upon whom the decree had been pronounced kept swarming and diminishing and passing away, unlike the rest of the camp who were among them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Ladino/Spanish word 'אסטורדידו״ס' (astordidos, 'bewildered/confounded') is rendered in parentheses alongside the Hebrew 'הומים'; the cryptic phrase 'בל״ס' is resolved as an abbreviation for 'בל\"ג שנים' or similar, here translated as 'in the thirty-eight years' following the context of the wilderness wandering."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:33.052562617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}